<title>USA: Harman files $150 mln shelf of debt.</title>
<headline>Harman files $150 mln shelf of debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harman International Industries Inc filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf offering of up to $150 million of senior notes due 2007.</p>
<p>Underwriters for the offering are Chase Securities Inc, NationsBanc Capital Markets Inc, Lehman Brothers Inc, Montgomery Securities and Societe Generale Securities Corp.</p>
<p>Procees from the sale will be used to repay outstanding debt and for other general corporate needs, the company said in the filing.</p>
</text>
